// frob.strata -- frob's own architecture, modeled in its own language
// (phase 4 self-hosting exit criterion, T-0081, docs/strata/roadmap.md
// "Self-hosting commitments (decision D7)"). This supersedes the informal
// module-dependency diagram in docs/rework.md as enforced truth: `frob
// check --only sys` gates on the directives below resolving into THIS
// model, on (T-0080) cross-component imports respecting the flows
// declared here wherever tier-2 `code=` binding is in force, and (T-0150)
// on each node's `code`/`may` declarations below matching what `frob sys
// audit`'s SYS100/SYS101/SYS102 self-conformance checks actually observe
// in `src/frob/`.
//
// Every node below declares `code "<glob>" ...;` (tier-2 code binding,
// T-0078/T-0132) and `may "<capability>";` (declared capability surface,
// T-0079/T-0132) directly -- both ARE reachable from `.strata` source text
// today (T-0132 landed the STRING-quoted `code`/`may` grammar in
// `strata-core/src/parse.rs::parse_node`, `docs/strata/surface.md#node-
// grammar-implemented-t-0132-closes-the-code-may-gap-t-0136-adds-on-
// deploy`). A PRIOR version of this file's header claimed otherwise --
// that claim was already stale when written (T-0132 landed before this
// file's merge-base) and has been corrected here; see T-0150's Done
// report for the full correction record. `may` values were measured
// honestly via `frob.vet._capability.scan_file_capabilities` against every
// file each node's `code` globs bind (T-0150); a "may" atom's kind is the
// segment before its first `.`/`:` (`_effects.py::_may_kind`), so a bare
// kind name like `"net"`/`"fs"`/`"exec"` (the same three names THREAT004's
// `_KIND_MAP` already normalizes net/fs-write/exec sinks to) or
// `"eval"`/`"env"`/`"ffi"`/`"install-hook"` (vet's own kind names, which
// have no tier-2 line-level analog -- T-0150's SYS100 extended case) is
// declared as-is.
//
// Every flow below is a real import edge this repo's `src/frob/*`
// packages actually have today (computed by walking `from frob.X import`/
// `import frob.X` across every file and rolling the 25+ leaf packages up
// into the 8 components docs/strata/roadmap.md names for phase 4:
// cli/app layer, graph+lang, gates, tickets, check, strata, dup+frob-core,
// vet). Where two components import each other in both directions, both
// flows are declared -- this model does not pretend the real dependency
// graph is a DAG when it is not.
//
// PII posture (T-0154, std.pii): EXPLICITLY ZERO. frob processes design
// text, ticket text, and code -- not personal data. No node/store below
// declares `carries "<category>.<field>"`, and that absence is checked,
// not assumed: `tests/unit/strata/test_pii.py::
// TestFrobSelfModelPiiPosture` asserts zero `pii=` attrs on every node
// here AND that `_pii.py::evaluate_pii` reports zero PII001-004
// violations, so a future edit that silently starts modeling personal
// data (e.g. a `registry` node gaining an author-email store) fails that
// test loudly rather than the zero case just happening to hold by
// omission. The one genuinely personal datum anywhere near this repo --
// git commit author name/email -- is process/VCS metadata `git` itself
// already records outside `design/`'s scope entirely, the same reasoning
// every other node's `attrs` already applies to "things this model does
// not represent" (docs/strata/threat.md#compliance zero-case precedent:
// an explicit exclusion, never a silent one).

// frob:doc docs/strata/roadmap.md#self-hosting-commitments-decision-d7
module frob

// -- components --------------------------------------------------------

// The only foreign-trust node: third-party package registries (PyPI/npm/
// crates.io/OSV) that `frob.vet` queries over the network
// (src/frob/vet/_registry.py, _osv.py, _popular_*.py). Nothing else in
// this model talks to the network.
// frob:doc docs/strata/roadmap.md#self-hosting-commitments-decision-d7
node registry : foreign { clearance Public; }

// cli/app layer: src/frob/__main__.py, src/frob/app/**. The single
// entrypoint every subcommand dispatches through (app.py's
// `_dispatch_table`); every other component is reached only via a runner
// in this layer. `may`: T-0150 measured `eval` (bare `compile(` matches --
// see the filed T-0151-class scanner-precision ticket in this ticket's
// Done report, not fixed here) and `fs.write` (T-0717 mode-qualified
// spelling; config/log file writes) across every file `code` binds.
// frob:doc docs/strata/roadmap.md#self-hosting-commitments-decision-d7
// frob:ticket T-0956
// frob:ticket T-1410
// frob:ticket T-1501
// frob:waive AFFECT001 reason="T-1113/T-1501: mechanical interface= attr population \
// (measured public-surface metadata for the mandatory SYS104 check), not a \
// behavioral/architectural change -- the cited affects()-closure doc does not \
// describe this node's public surface and has nothing to update here."
// frob:ticket T-1644
node cli : trusted {
    attr interface=[
        ARCH_DEFAULT_GOD_MODULE_MIN_CLUSTERS, ARCH_DEFAULT_GOD_MODULE_MIN_EXPORTS, ARCH_DEFAULT_LCOM4_MIN_FIELD_USING_METHODS, ARCH_DEFAULT_LCOM4_MIN_METHODS, ARCH_DEFAULT_MAX_CLASS_METHODS, ARCH_DEFAULT_MAX_FILE_LINES,
        ARCH_DEFAULT_MAX_FUNCTION_LINES, ARCH_DEFAULT_MAX_LOCAL_IMPORTS, ARCH_DEFAULT_MAX_NESTING_DEPTH, ARCH_DEFAULT_MIXED_CONCERN_MIN_DECISION_POINTS, AppConfig, DoctorReport,
        LiveLandProcess, NativeExtensionStatus, ProxyReason, RapidSweepError, STATE_STYLE, Subcommand,
        TELEMETRY_REL, Tip, _accept, _add_release_parser, _add_test_parser, _add_ticket_land_parser,
        _apply_evidence, _block, _brief, _check_gates_summary_fn, _close, _close_failure_hint,
        _doable, _done_report, _drop, _evidence, _fail, _kind,
        _land, _land_collected_fn, _land_passed_fn, _list, _log_evidence_result, _merge_driver,
        _new, _render_acceptance, _reverify, _review, _run_pytest_directly, _run_tests_count_fn,
        _scope, _scope_ack, _show, _start, _work, append_event,
        detect_footguns, ensure_daemon, estimate_tokens, fast_yaml_loader, is_disabled, is_excluded,
        is_skipped_dir, is_test_file, iso_now, iter_files, land_parity_findings, load_arch_config,
        load_exclude_globs, query, read_toml_lenient, record_cli_event, record_ticket_event, redact_command,
        release_daemon_lease, render_tips, run, run_deferred_post_land_sweep, run_diagnosis, scan_live_land_processes,
        scan_venv_shims, spawn_deferred_post_land_sweep, stale_binary_warning, stale_install_warning, style_fail, style_header,
        style_ok, style_rule, style_state, style_ticket_id, style_warn, timed_call,
        tips_disabled, tree_hash, try_daemon_lease, usage_report, verify_derived_state, walk_pruned,
    ];
    clearance Internal;
    // T-0500 (docs/audits/strata.md G4): src/frob/__init__.py (package
    // glue re-exporting gitio/excludes, T-0362), src/frob/doctor.py (the
    // `frob doctor` diagnostic subcommand), and src/frob/excludes.py
    // (scan-exclusion helpers used repo-wide) are loose top-level files
    // with no subdirectory of their own -- tightening SYS102 to fire per
    // FOREIGN file (not just per fully-foreign top-level directory)
    // surfaced that none of the three had ever been given a code= glob
    // owner at all. `cli` already owns __main__.py, the other single-file
    // top-level entrypoint, so it is the existing-convention home for
    // this class of file rather than inventing a new node for three
    // small files.
    // T-1076: __main__.py's own _add_*_parser argparse builders split out
    // into src/frob/_cli_parsers/** (a package, same T-1072/T-0989 pattern
    // as the earlier gates/_pii_structural split) -- still the same cli
    // entrypoint code, just no longer a single file.
    code "src/frob/app/**" "src/frob/__main__.py" "src/frob/__init__.py" "src/frob/yaml_io.py"
        "src/frob/_cli_parsers/**"
        "src/frob/doctor.py" "src/frob/excludes.py" "src/frob/tomlio.py";
    may "eval" via "src/frob/doctor.py";
    may "fs.write" via "src/frob/app/_check_chunking.py", "src/frob/app/_config_external.py", "src/frob/app/_config_meta.py", "src/frob/app/_daemon_proxy.py", "src/frob/app/check_runner.py", "src/frob/app/debt_runner.py", "src/frob/app/deploy_runner.py", "src/frob/app/exports_runner.py", "src/frob/app/release_runner.py", "src/frob/app/sys_runner.py", "src/frob/app/telemetry.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_land_cmd.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_lifecycle.py", "src/frob/doctor.py", "src/frob/excludes.py", "src/frob/tomlio.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_rapid_sweep.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_close_cmd.py";
    may "fs.read" via "src/frob/app/_check_chunking.py", "src/frob/app/deploy_runner.py", "src/frob/app/parse_runner.py", "src/frob/app/perf_runner.py", "src/frob/app/sys_runner.py", "src/frob/app/telemetry.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_close_cmd.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_land_cmd.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_mutate.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_new.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_verify.py", "src/frob/doctor.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_rapid_sweep.py";
    // T-0178: frob.app.telemetry reads FROB_NO_TELEMETRY/FROB_STATS_AGENTIC
    // (os.environ.get) to opt out of/into the non-gated agentic telemetry
    // stream and its `--agentic` report trigger. T-1535: _land_cmd.py's
    // land_parity_findings reads os.environ to build the spawned check's
    // env (FROB_NO_GATE_CACHE injection) -- folded into this bare `env`
    // declaration rather than a separate `env.read` atom (T-1589: the
    // narrower kind expands to a strict subset of what this bare
    // declaration already covers, so a standalone atom for it is never
    // mutation-audit load-bearing).
    may "env" via "src/frob/app/_daemon_proxy.py", "src/frob/app/check_runner.py", "src/frob/app/stats_runner.py", "src/frob/app/telemetry.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_land_cmd.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_verify.py";
    // T-0474: `frob ticket start` detaches its pre-work sweep as a
    // background `frob ticket sweep` child (subprocess.Popen of
    // sys.executable in app/ticket_runner.py::_spawn_background_sweep).
    // Same T-0200 discipline as the checker node: the spawn honors the
    // real, live FROB_DISABLE_EXEC kill switch (frob.process._guard.
    // exec_enabled) by degrading to the synchronous in-process sweep, so
    // this is a switchable capability, not an aspirational claim.
    may "exec" via "src/frob/app/_daemon_proxy.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_close_cmd.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_land_cmd.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_lifecycle.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_verify.py", "src/frob/app/ticket_runner/_rapid_sweep.py";
    // T-1126: the CLI daemon proxy (app/_daemon_proxy.py) now opens the
    // project daemon's unix socket directly for lease acquire/release
    // (_LeaseConnection, promoted from the T-1097 test-only _RawClient)
    // in addition to the query path -- a local AF_UNIX connect to the
    // T-1092 socket under the project state dir, never a remote network
    // endpoint; degrades to the in-process/file-lock fallback when no
    // daemon is up.
    may "net" via "src/frob/app/_daemon_proxy.py";
    attr flag=frob_check_exec_kill_switch;
    // T-0724: SYS203 (shared store write) fires because cli/core/fleet/
    // gates/serve all have a Flow into tickets_ledger -- correctly, per
    // the grammar's mode-blind "any inbound flow counts as a write"
    // framing (docs/strata/host.md#resource-contention-sys2xx-t-0699).
    // T-0956: the ledger's real arbiter -- every writer serializes
    // through the `.frob/tickets.lock` flock (T-0458 single-writer CLI,
    // hardened by T-0633's locked wholesale ops) -- is now a model-level
    // fact too (`resource tickets_ledger { lock "tickets.lock"; }` below,
    // plus this node's own `access "tickets_ledger" mode write;`), and
    // SYS204's mode-aware `resource_contention_violations` proof confirms
    // it discharges cleanly. T-1025 taught `check_resource_contention`
    // (SYS203) to consult the same arbiter given a `module=` argument;
    // T-1146 wired that argument into the LIVE SELFAUDIT001/`frob sys
    // audit` call sites, so SYS203 now genuinely discharges here too --
    // the `waive "SYS203:tickets_ledger" ...` clause this comment used to
    // justify is REMOVED (it went stale the moment that wiring landed,
    // verified via `frob sys audit`'s own stale-waiver detection).
    access "tickets_ledger" mode write;
    // T-1158: SYS205 WRITE path-scoping now discharges cleanly via a
    // real owns= claim -- T-1164 fixed the blast-radius false positive
    // this declaration would otherwise have triggered (bare runs_as=None
    // treated as a compromised-user identity), and T-1146/T-1149 wired
    // module= into the live check_resource_contention call so SYS201
    // stays arbiter-aware for this owns= claim (tickets_ledger's shared
    // lock, verified: `frob sys audit` clean with no new SYS201/SYS205
    // findings). The `waive "SYS205:tickets_ledger" ...` clause this
    // comment used to justify is REMOVED.
    owns "tickets.md" "0644";
}

// graph+lang: src/frob/graph/**, src/frob/lang/**, src/frob/arch/**. Owns
// parsing (tree-sitter walkers + the strata-core native module), the
// symbol graph snapshot, and per-language digest extraction that every
// other component reads.
// T-0158: `may "sql"` added -- graph/cache.py's sqlite cache writer matches
// the registry's python/sql DangerousOperation (string-formatted
// cursor.execute), a real (if benign, parameterization-owned) observed
// capability the new exhaustive registry now surfaces that the coarser
// old pattern table never patterned.
// frob:doc docs/strata/roadmap.md#self-hosting-commitments-decision-d7
// frob:waive AFFECT001 reason="T-1113: mechanical interface= attr population \
// (measured public-surface metadata for the new mandatory SYS104 check), not a \
// behavioral/architectural change -- the cited affects()-closure doc does not \
// describe this node's public surface and has nothing to update here."
node graphlang : trusted {

    attr interface=[
        ArchCategory, BuildError, COMMENT_TYPES, CacheLocked, CallGraph, Digests,
        DischargeResult, Edge, EdgeKind, FACETS, FacetState, FacetStatus,
        FunctionSummary, GraphError, GraphSnapshot, KNOWN_GAP_TRACKING_TICKETS, KotlinAdapter, LangError,
        LanguageAdapter, LanguageSupport, LayeringConfig, LockEntry, LockError, LockFile,
        NATIVE_UNAVAILABLE_MESSAGE, NormalizedBranch, NormalizedCall, NormalizedCallArg, NormalizedCatch, NormalizedClass,
        NormalizedField, NormalizedFieldAccess, NormalizedFunction, NormalizedImport, NormalizedLoop, NormalizedModule,
        NormalizedParam, NormalizedRaise, NormalizedReturn, NormalizedSubscript, ParseFailure, ParsedFile,
        PythonAdapter, RawComment, RawSymbol, RustAdapter, SummaryResult, SymbolId,
        SymbolKind, SymbolRecord, TreeNode, TypeScriptAdapter, UNKNOWN, UNRESOLVED_CALLEE,
        WAIVE_PRESETS, _digest_body, _digest_doc, _digest_sig, acknowledge, affects,
        analyze_project, build_call_graph, build_graph, build_ordered_call_graph, build_reference_graph, check_boolean_flag_param,
        check_data_clumps, check_dead_private_code, check_deep_inheritance, check_errors_as_values, check_fat_interface, check_feature_envy,
        check_god_module, check_illegal_states_representable, check_layering_violations, check_lcom4, check_magic_literal, check_mixed_concern_function,
        check_module_dependency_cycles, check_mutable_default_arg, check_narrow_client_usage, check_no_di_construction, check_noop_override, check_over_broad_except,
        check_override_raises_not_implemented, check_override_signature_variance, check_override_strengthened_precondition, check_override_weakened_postcondition, check_parse_dont_validate, check_primitive_obsession,
        check_print_as_diagnostic, check_recoverable_error_wrong_signature, check_swallowed_exception, check_temporal_coupling, check_unhandled_result, check_unlogged_boundary,
        check_unlogged_error_path, child_by_field, closure, compute_digests, compute_may_raise, compute_protocol_summaries,
        conformance_violations, core_available, cpp_function_nodes, cpp_raii_discharge, dedupe_slug, derive_language_registry,
        drift, edges_from, edges_to, export_tree, extract_imports, flatten_tree,
        fold_comment_runs, gc_finalizer_discharge, is_generated_source, is_symref, iter_identifiers, load_graph,
        load_layering_config, load_lock, markdown_anchors, node_text, parse_cache_stats, parse_directives,
        parse_file, parse_kotlin, parse_pyi_declared_raises, partial_parse_files, python_with_discharge, raw_kotlin_tree,
        raw_tree, reset_parse_cache, resolve, resolve_call_edges_native, resolve_local_import, resolve_preset,
        run_fallibility_checks, run_isp_checks, run_logging_checks, run_lsp_checks, run_smell_checks, run_srp_checks,
        run_typedesign_checks, rust_drop_discharge, scan_ctypes_boundary_calls, scan_pyo3_raises, scope_doc_code_gaps, scope_private_helper_gaps,
        scope_test_gaps, slugify, supported_languages, symbol_tree, typescript_using_discharge, walk_strata,
        write_lock,
    ];
    clearance Internal;
    code "src/frob/graph/**" "src/frob/lang/**" "src/frob/arch/**";
    may "eval" via "src/frob/arch/_layering.py", "src/frob/lang/_walk_strata.py";
    may "fs.write" via "src/frob/arch/_layering.py", "src/frob/arch/_lock_ordering.py", "src/frob/graph/_generated.py", "src/frob/graph/cache.py", "src/frob/graph/lock.py";
    may "fs.read" via "src/frob/arch/__init__.py", "src/frob/arch/_layering.py", "src/frob/arch/_python.py", "src/frob/graph/__init__.py", "src/frob/graph/lock.py", "src/frob/lang/__init__.py";
    // T-1464: `_artifact_cache_connection` reads `PARSE_ARTIFACT_CACHE_ENV`
    // (an owning `ProcessPoolExecutor` parent's own stamped filesystem
    // path, see `frob.gates._stamp_worker_parse_artifact_cache_env`) to
    // find the shared persistent parse-artifact cache -- a plain
    // os.environ.get, not a secret or untrusted input.
    may "env.read" via "src/frob/lang/__init__.py";
    may "sql" via "src/frob/graph/cache.py";
    // T-0845: graph_cache's fill/invalidation flows are `_infra.py::
    // _cache_node_and_fill_flow`/`_cache_invalidation_flow_for`-
    // synthesized edges. They now carry `_infra.py::_CACHE_LOCAL_ATTR`
    // (`"local"`) unconditionally -- an explicit local disposition for
    // every `cache` construct's in-process in-memory flows (chosen over
    // a per-flow `attr` grammar clause, which would need a strata-core
    // parser change outside this ticket's scope) -- so REL200 no longer
    // fires on them and the prior waivers are burned down.
}

// gates: src/frob/gates/**. The obligation-graph rule engine (SYS/DRIFT/
// COV/task-tracking/etc.); reads graph+lang's snapshot and strata's design models,
// writes nothing on its own (violations are reported, not auto-filed --
// T-0086's `frob sys plan` is the future ticket-filing seam).
// T-0151: `may "eval"` REMOVED here. It was measured from vet's capability
// scanner matching bare `compile(` against this package's `re.compile(`
// calls (_FRONTMATTER_RE, _AD_ID_RE, _TODO_RE, etc -- all regex, zero real
// eval/exec/dynamic-import anywhere in src/frob/gates/**, confirmed by
// direct grep). The scanner's `compile(` needle now only counts a BARE
// builtin call (T-0151, src/frob/vet/_capability.py), so this package no
// longer observes "eval" and the declaration would otherwise be a stale,
// unfalsifiable claim -- exactly what SYS101 exists to catch.
// frob:doc docs/strata/roadmap.md#self-hosting-commitments-decision-d7
// T-1318: `frob.security` (src/frob/security/**) -- lightweight, `frob.
// gates`-independent security primitives. Split out of `frob.gates._secrets`
// specifically so importing the secret-token detection engine (regex/
// entropy/redaction) never pays `frob.gates/__init__.py`'s eager
// whole-package stage-roster import cost; `frob.app.telemetry.
// redact_command` (a per-CLI-invocation call site) and `frob.gates.
// _secrets` (the gate itself) both import FROM this module now, not the
// other way around. No `may` capabilities: this module is pure regex/
// string logic over an in-memory token, no filesystem, process, network,
// or env access of its own -- see `frob.security._redact`'s module
// docstring for the extraction's full rationale.
// frob:doc docs/modules/gates.md#structural-pii-secrets-detection-t-0207
// frob:ticket T-1318
node security : trusted {
    attr interface=[
        _FAKE_MARKER_REASON_RE, _PATTERNS, _SecretPattern, _redact, _scan_line,
    ];
    clearance Internal;
    code "src/frob/security/**";
}

// frob:ticket T-1687
// frob:ticket T-1688
// frob:doc \
// docs/modules/tickets.md#verification-watermark-t-1687-foundation-of-the-t-1686-epic
node verify : trusted {
    attr interface=[
        CoalescingWorker, WatermarkError, WorkerError, WorkerOutcome, advance_watermark, compact_queue,
        load_watermark, queue_status, record_intent, run_coalesced_verification,
    ];
    clearance Internal;
    code "src/frob/verify/**";
    may "fs.write" via "src/frob/verify/_watermark.py";
    may "fs.read" via "src/frob/verify/_watermark.py";
}

// frob:ticket T-0956
// frob:ticket T-1227
// frob:ticket T-1262
// frob:ticket T-1263
// frob:ticket T-1340
// frob:doc docs/strata/roadmap.md#self-hosting-commitments-decision-d7
// frob:waive AFFECT001 reason="T-1113: mechanical interface= attr population \
// (measured public-surface metadata for the new mandatory SYS104 check), not a \
// behavioral/architectural change -- the cited affects()-closure doc does not \
// describe this node's public surface and has nothing to update here."
// frob:ticket T-1548
node gates : trusted {

    attr interface=[
        ALL_PROVIDERS, CoverageData, DecisionError, DeprecatedBaselineEntry, DeprecatedBaselineLock, FIELD_SIGNATURES,
        FixApplied, GateConfig, GateError, GateReport, GateStats, Invariant,
        InvariantError, PERF_REACH_DEGRADED_SKIP_MARKER, PreworkSweep, REGISTRY_FILES, RatchetError, SCOPED_RUN_FLAKY_RULE_IDS,
        Severity, SuppressionDialect, SystemSpec, TIER_A_HANDLERS, TestPolicy, TrackedSnapshot,
        Violation, WaiverRef, _Criticality, _DecisionStatus, _UNWAIVABLE_RULES, _is_data_structure,
        _is_email_shaped, _load_declared_surface, _match_waiver, _redact, _scan_python_ddl, _scan_python_email_values,
        _scan_python_env_access, _scan_python_fields, _scan_python_keyword_sweep, _waive006_binding_ticket_refs, _waive006_comment_violations, _waive006_strata_violations,
        _waive007_comment_violations, _waive007_is_exempt_dangling_ref, _waive007_strata_violations, active_ticket, affect_drift_gate, apply_tier_a_fixes,
        apply_tier_b_fixes, apply_tier_c_fixits, arch_gate, bug_repro_violations, cache_gate, canonicalize_text,
        clear_autofix_manifest, clear_ratchet_entry, compliance_gate, coverage_gate, coverage_lock_diff, cve_fingerprint_scan_gate,
        dead_symbol_gate, debt_gate, decisions_gate, delta_violations, deprecated_current_references, deprecated_gate,
        doc004_gate, doc005_gate, doc006_gate, docanchor_gate, docenum001_gate, doclink_gate,
        docmake_gate, docstatus_gate, drift_gate, dup_gate, evaluate_cacheable_gate, evidence_covers_scope,
        exclude_hazard_gate, exhaustive_handling_gate, extra_key, fake_marker_staleness_gate, ffi_boundary_gate, file_reference_counts,
        find_exclusivity_claim_sentences, fix_cov002_ticket_directive_insertion, fix_e501_merge_introduced, fix_fmt001_directive_wrap, fix_reg010_registry_sync, fix_rel002_release_sync,
        fix_suppress001_paired_suppression, fix_tick002_renumber, fix_waive004_stale_waiver, fmt_gate, format_paths, fuzz_gate,
        generated_gate_rule_ids, inv003_gate, inv004_gate, inv006_gate, inv007_violations, inv008_violations,
        invalidate, invariant_gate, is_baseline_stale, known_gate_rule_ids, lang_conformance_gate, list_debt,
        list_deprecated, load_baseline, load_coverage, load_coverage_lock, load_decisions, load_deprecated_baseline,
        load_invariants, load_lock_audit_log, load_prework, load_ratchet_lock, load_root_gate_cache, load_stamp,
        marker_for, model_side_channel_key, mutation_evidence_violations, negexist001_gate, opaque_gate, parse_failure_gate,
        path_ever_tracked, perf_gate, pii_structural_gate, prework_gate, project_lang_conformance_gate, protocol_summary_gate,
        ratchet_enabled_rules, read_line_length, record_prework, ref_gate, registry_gate, release_gate,
        render_lint_gate, resolve_ratchet_severity, root_content_key, run_gates, save_deprecated_baseline, scan_emitted_rule_ids,
        scope_digest, scope_gate, secrets_gate, snapshot_ratchet, stamp_baseline, stamp_coverage,
        store_root_gate_cache, strip_code_spans, suppress001_gate, suppression_dialects, sweep_ticket, sys_gate,
        taint_gate, test_gate, ticket_lease_pin, tickets_gate, tighten_deprecated_baseline, violation_fingerprint,
        waive006_gate, waive007_gate, walk_lint_gate, wire_gate, write_autofix_manifest, write_coverage_lock,
    ];
    clearance Internal;
    code "src/frob/gates/**";
    // T-0207: `_pii_structural.py` (the SEC110 detector) references
    // `os.environ`/`os.getenv` as the scan-pattern data it matches AGAINST
    // -- the capability scanner observes an `env` capability there. Declared
    // honestly-to-the-measurement (a sound may-analysis over-approximation:
    // the scanner cannot prove gates never reads env), matching how every
    // other node's `may` set is measured from `scan_directory_capabilities`.
    may "env" via "src/frob/gates/__init__.py", "src/frob/gates/_cache_gate.py", "src/frob/gates/_mutation_evidence.py", "src/frob/gates/_pii_structural/_env_access.py", "src/frob/gates/_tickets_gate.py";
    may "fs.write" via "src/frob/gates/__init__.py", "src/frob/gates/_baseline.py", "src/frob/gates/_coverage.py", "src/frob/gates/_deprecated_baseline.py", "src/frob/gates/_docblocks.py", "src/frob/gates/_doclink_docanchor.py", "src/frob/gates/_docptr.py", "src/frob/gates/_dup.py", "src/frob/gates/_fix_engine.py", "src/frob/gates/_fix_engine_shared.py", "src/frob/gates/_fix_engine_sync.py", "src/frob/gates/_fix_engine_text.py", "src/frob/gates/_fix_engine_tier_b.py", "src/frob/gates/_fmt_directives.py", "src/frob/gates/_fuzz.py", "src/frob/gates/_gate_cache.py", "src/frob/gates/_mutation_evidence.py", "src/frob/gates/_prework.py", "src/frob/gates/_ratchet.py", "src/frob/gates/_refs.py", "src/frob/gates/_render_lint.py", "src/frob/gates/_sys.py", "src/frob/gates/_tickets_gate.py", "src/frob/gates/_todo_fmt.py", "src/frob/gates/_waive.py", "src/frob/gates/_wire.py";
    may "fs.read" via "src/frob/gates/__init__.py", "src/frob/gates/_baseline.py", "src/frob/gates/_cache_gate.py", "src/frob/gates/_coverage.py", "src/frob/gates/_cve_fingerprint_scan.py", "src/frob/gates/_dead_symbols.py", "src/frob/gates/_debt_deprecated.py", "src/frob/gates/_deprecated_baseline.py", "src/frob/gates/_docblocks.py", "src/frob/gates/_docblocks_refs.py", "src/frob/gates/_docenum.py", "src/frob/gates/_doclink_docanchor.py", "src/frob/gates/_docptr.py", "src/frob/gates/_exclude_hazard.py", "src/frob/gates/_exhaustive_handling.py", "src/frob/gates/_ffi_boundary.py", "src/frob/gates/_fix_engine.py", "src/frob/gates/_fix_engine_shared.py", "src/frob/gates/_fix_engine_sync.py", "src/frob/gates/_fix_engine_text.py", "src/frob/gates/_fix_engine_tier_b.py", "src/frob/gates/_fmt_directives.py", "src/frob/gates/_gate_cache.py", "src/frob/gates/_inv.py", "src/frob/gates/_inv006_split_assist.py", "src/frob/gates/_pii_structural/__init__.py", "src/frob/gates/_prework.py", "src/frob/gates/_protocol_summary.py", "src/frob/gates/_ratchet.py", "src/frob/gates/_refs.py", "src/frob/gates/_registry_exhaustiveness.py", "src/frob/gates/_render_lint.py", "src/frob/gates/_rule_id_scan.py", "src/frob/gates/_secrets.py", "src/frob/gates/_suppress.py", "src/frob/gates/_sys.py", "src/frob/gates/_tickets_gate.py", "src/frob/gates/_waive_comments.py", "src/frob/gates/_walk_lint.py", "src/frob/gates/_wire.py", "src/frob/gates/decisions.py", "src/frob/gates/invariants.py";
    // T-0443: the DOC004 console/bash command-drift tier resolves the
    // `[[docblocks.commands]]` parser source by dotted path via
    // importlib.import_module (gates/_docblocks.py) -- a dynamic-import
    // (eval-family) capability the scanner rightly observes. The import
    // target comes from tracked frob.toml, not user input, and failures
    // fail open to the unbound warning path.
    may "eval" via "src/frob/gates/_docblocks_refs.py";
    // T-0956/T-1146: same SYS203/tickets_ledger disposition as `cli`
    // above -- SYS203 now genuinely discharges live here too (the
    // `waive "SYS203:tickets_ledger" ...` clause this comment used to
    // justify is REMOVED; see `cli`'s full comment above for the
    // reasoning).
    access "tickets_ledger" mode write;
    // T-1158: SYS205 WRITE path-scoping now discharges cleanly via a
    // real owns= claim -- T-1164 fixed the blast-radius false positive
    // this declaration would otherwise have triggered (bare runs_as=None
    // treated as a compromised-user identity), and T-1146/T-1149 wired
    // module= into the live check_resource_contention call so SYS201
    // stays arbiter-aware for this owns= claim (tickets_ledger's shared
    // lock, verified: `frob sys audit` clean with no new SYS201/SYS205
    // findings). The `waive "SYS205:tickets_ledger" ...` clause this
    // comment used to justify is REMOVED.
    owns "tickets.md" "0644";
}

// check orchestration: src/frob/check/**. Runs the gate suite plus the
// process-spawned tool integrations (ruff/mypy/pytest via `frob.process`)
// and folds results into one exit code.
// T-0200 (closing T-0155's honest LINT004 gap): `may "exec"` now has a
// REAL, checked-in kill switch -- `frob.process._guard.
// guarded_subprocess_run` (`src/frob/process/_guard.py`), an env-var-gated
// wrapper every `_run_*` tool runner in `src/frob/check/_python.py`/
// `_native.py`/`_ts.py` calls instead of `subprocess.run` directly.
// Setting `FROB_DISABLE_EXEC=1` genuinely stops every process this
// component spawns (`tests/unit/test_process_guard.py`), live and without
// a redeploy -- this is no longer an aspirational claim (T-0150/T-0151
// discipline: `attr flag=<id>` names an identifier that is real, not a
// mechanism that does not exist), so the T-0174 `waive "LINT004"` is
// retired in favor of the real declaration below.
// frob:doc docs/strata/roadmap.md#self-hosting-commitments-decision-d7
// frob:waive AFFECT001 reason="T-1113: mechanical interface= attr population \
// (measured public-surface metadata for the new mandatory SYS104 check), not a \
// behavioral/architectural change -- the cited affects()-closure doc does not \
// describe this node's public surface and has nothing to update here."
node checker : trusted {

    attr interface=[
        CheckResult, available_stages, detect_project_type, memoize_per_run, reset_run_memo, run_check,
        run_check_cpp, run_check_rust, run_check_ts, run_memo_scope, run_memo_stats,
    ];
    clearance Internal;
    code "src/frob/check/**";
    // T-1346: _python.py's FROB_NO_GATE_CACHE feature-flag read (the gate
    // result cache escape hatch) -- a boolean opt-out, no secret carried.
    may "env.read";
    may "exec";
    may "fs.write";
    may "fs.read";
    attr flag=frob_check_exec_kill_switch;
}

// strata itself: src/frob/strata/**, strata-core/**. Parses/elaborates/
// evaluates `.strata` design models (this file included) and does tier-2
// code-binding/effect extraction, which is why it depends on `vet`'s
// capability pattern tables (`_effects.py` reuses `frob.vet._capability`).
// `code` covers only the python half (`strata-core/**`'s rust source is
// outside `bind_code`'s `*.py` walk, T-0078 scope).
// T-0769: `may "net"` (formerly here, T-0155/T-0174's LINT004 waiver
// pending T-0200's kill switch) is DROPPED -- a strictness-increasing
// narrowing, not a relaxation. T-0769's docstring/comment-prose exclusion
// fix proved this module's `net` capability was NEVER genuinely observed
// on real code; the only thing that ever satisfied SYS101 here was a
// docstring false positive in `_effects.py`'s own module docstring
// (`requests.post(...)`-shaped prose describing a hypothetical example),
// now reworded. A direct scan of every file under `src/frob/strata/**`
// confirms zero real net-capable code today. If this package genuinely
// grows a net-capable call in the future, `may "net"` must be
// re-declared then, together with a real kill-switch mechanism (T-0200)
// -- not carried forward speculatively on the strength of a false
// positive. See T-draft-22aa6efc for the discovery/investigation this
// narrowing resolves.
// frob:doc docs/strata/roadmap.md#self-hosting-commitments-decision-d7
// frob:waive AFFECT001 reason="T-1113: mechanical interface= attr population \
// (measured public-surface metadata for the new mandatory SYS104 check), not a \
// behavioral/architectural change -- the cited affects()-closure doc does not \
// describe this node's public surface and has nothing to update here."
